  balanceRequests:
  - title: "Ship feel \u2014 fast & nimble"
    request: Ships should feel fast and nimble. Acceleration should make most average
      multi-engine/thruster fairly quick.
    enabled: 1
    priority: 90
  - title: Tier progression
    request: Low-level ships should be faster / more agile but less powerful than
      higher-level ships. Higher tiers trade some agility for firepower, cargo, and
      survivability.
    enabled: 1
    priority: 85
  - title: Capture with ~3 ships
    request: About 3 ships with average people capacity for their level should be
      able to capture an equal-level average-sized planet (full population) without
      needing a 10-ship zerg. Coordinate with planet population caps and unload batch
      sizes.
    enabled: 1
    priority: 95
  - title: Planet regen pace
    request: "Planet population regeneration must not be too fast \u2014 freshly
      captured empty planets should stay vulnerable long enough for counter-play
      (current FullRefillSeconds \u2248 120s is a baseline)."
    enabled: 1
    priority: 70
  - title: Asteroid combat loop
    request: "Mid asteroids should take roughly 8\u201312 seconds for a median L1
      DPS ship to kill. Gem capacity vs mining rate should support active loops,
      not instant full cargo."
    enabled: 1
    priority: 80
  - title: Energy complementarity
    request: "Engines are the energy source; weapons spend energy to fire; overdrive
      bursts spend energy for speed. Sustained fire must drain the pool (regen below
      firePower\xD7fireRate). Cards are sidegrades, not a second engine stack."
    enabled: 1
    priority: 75
  - title: Power score cargo weight
    request: "Gem capacity must not dominate ship power score vs firepower \u2014
      keep gem power contribution \u2248 rawGems/10, people \u2248 rawPeople/4, so
      upgrade trees sort by combat+mobility meaningfully."
    enabled: 1
    priority: 65
  - title: Ship's health vs energy cap/regen vs firing power/rate ratio and sustained
      fire.
    request: Ships should have enough avg energy capacity to sustain avg firing of
      bullets so that we get about 3 seconds of full firing, and energy regen balance
      it to 30% of how much that weapon consumes. This is mainly between the engine
      and weapon components to compliment each other. We need to also balance fire
      power to ship health. There should be enough avg health cap to sustain 3 seconds
      of avg dps.
    enabled: 1
    priority: 95
  sessionNotes: "2\u20135 teams \xD7 ~20 players, domination matches ~0.5\u20132
    hours. Capture all planets to win. Balance ship levels vs planet levels vs turrets."
  lastReviewUtc: 2026-08-11 16:00:37Z
  lastChassisCount: 241
  lastReviewSummary: "# GameBalanceTargets\n\n- Session: 2\u20135 teams \xD7 20 players,
    ~30\u2013120 min domination\n- Capture: 3 ships \xD7 5 batches; home pop\u2248129
    \u2192 L3 peopleCap\u22488.6 (L1\u22487.2)\n- Cargo parts assumption: 1 cockpit
    + 2 wings (median cargo\u22483) \u2192 people/part V1=1.70 (capture-tuned), gems/part
    V1\u224820.00 (gemCap target\xF72 L1 cargo parts)\n- Mid asteroid Size 35: TTK
    8\u201312s (ideal 10s); gem fill loop 45\u201390s\n- Target L1 gemCap\u224840;
    chassis cost = 2\xD7gemCap (\u22482 cargo trips)\n- Energy: Cap \u2248 3s of
    fire; regen fraction of sustained drain = 0.30; insolvency below 0.20\n- Health:
    \u2248 3s of own DPS (L1 target\u224827, part V1\u22486.75)\n- Attribute upgrade
    cost = shipLevel \xD7 5\n\r\nReviewed 241 chassis at 2026-08-11 16:00:37Z UTC.\r\nOutliers:
    134.\r\n\r\n### Economy\r\n- [PASS] mid_ttk_l1_sec = 10 (8-12)\r\n- [PASS] capture_batches
    = 4.97 (4-6)\r\n- [INFO] median_l3_people = 8.653 (8.6)\r\n- [PASS] median_l1_gemCap
    = 38.026 (40)\r\n- [PASS] median_wings = 2 (2)\r\n- [INFO] health_per_size =
    2.571 (AsteroidSettings)\r\n- [PASS] energy_cap_seconds_l1 = 3 (3)\r\n- [PASS]
    energy_regen_frac_l1 = 0.3 (0.3)\r\n- [PASS] health_seconds_of_dps_l1 = 3.808
    (3)\r\n- [INFO] gem_power_weight = raw/ 10 (power score only; purchase uses raw)\r\n"
